# Do not go to git on your own

Do not `git checkout`, `git restore`, `git reset`, or otherwise copy committed files onto the working tree unless the user explicitly asked.

New art is often untracked and never pushed. Git history is frequently older, not-16:9 PNG. Pulling it in overwrites current work.

Read-only git (`status`, `log`, `diff`, `ls-files`) is fine. Changing files from git is not, unless asked.
